\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. \cf0  My Saviour is on the Cross,
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 And at the point of death.
\par On the cross He stretched His arms
\par to welcome all the world.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par He stretch His hands, inviting us
\par He wants us be with Him.
\par Look at His strength of mercy
\par And the depth of His Love.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  With all my sinful action,
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 He nailed them to the cross.
\par And when my lust keeps pressing
\par and arrogance steps in.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par My Saviour keep advising,
\par Reminder of  the deed
\par that made me suffer for you;
\par and follow sin no more.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. If my work overloads me,
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0 and I become so slow,
\par then I remember His pains
\par and for all His sorrow.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\ulnone\b0 
\par His sufferings are so many\cf0 
\par And that so makes Him feel;
\par  So then I owe Him so much,
\par   I'll always give Him thanks.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4. O, I shall never forget
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj  My load He took away,
\par  And how my sinful actions
\par  have nailed Him to the tree!
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl200\slmult0\qj His ribs through where
\par they pierced Him,
\par  and I'll not go astray,
\par  that this new life He gave me,
\par \pard        I'll praise Him evermore!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

